<title>USA: Allendale sees US corn acres 80.92 mln, soy 66.47.</title>
<headline>Allendale sees US corn acres 80.92 mln, soy 66.47.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agricultural consultant Allendale Inc said its March planting intentions survey indicated U.S. farmers will plant 80.92 million acres to corn this summer and 66.47 million acres to soybeans.</p>
<p>Last year, U.S. farmers planted 79.5 million acres to corn and 64.2 million acres to soybeans, with production of 9.293 billion bushels of corn and 2.382 billion bushels of soybeans.</p>
<p>The survey of 16 leading producer states by the McHenry, Ill.-based Allendale also estimated 1997 cotton plantings at 14.30 million acres and wheat plantings at 69.25 million acres, with 44.76 million seeded to winter wheat.</p>
<p>U.S. wheat plantings last year totaled 75.6 million acres and cotton plantings 14.67 million acres.</p>
<p>USDA will release its first estimates of summer crop plantings on March 31.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
